<title>UK: Ewart says plans to change year-end.</title>
<headline>Ewart says plans to change year-end.</headline>
<dateline>BELFAST 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ewart Plc said on Friday that in order to bring the group into line with other quoted property companies in the UK and Ireland, whose year end falls in June or December, it plans changing its year-end date from 30 April to 30 June with effect from this financial year.</p>
<p>&quot;Consequently, our interim report this year will cover the 8 month period to 31 December 1996, while our final accounts will cover the 14 month period to 30 June 1997,&quot; Ewart said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Belfast Newsroom +44 1232 315253</p>
</text>
